# Nano mode (sys.gammaos.minimal_boot=1) starts class main but not late_start,
# which keeps the DRM home light. On this SoC the WCN3990 Wi-Fi needs
# cnss-daemon (class late_start in init.qcom.rc) for the firmware and QMI
# side: without it the cld driver never completes its configuration, the
# HAL's driver-state write fails with EINVAL and Wi-Fi cannot be enabled.
on property:sys.gammaos.minimal_boot=1
    start cnss-daemon

# Boot chime: the audio HAL service is class early_hal (late-fs, ~6.7 s) so it
# is registered by the time the sound card appears; the HAL itself waits for
# the card. The ADSP keeps its stock early-boot bring-up: booting it at
# late-fs, before pd-mapper and rmt_storage (class core, started at boot),
# left its audio services waiting and the card registered later, not earlier.


# Boot chime: the sound card only registers once the ADSP's audio services
# are up, and on this SoC those wait for the MODEM (the ADSP retries its modem
# SSR hand-shake until the modem is up). The modem is powered by per_proxy,
# which the stock rc starts with class core at boot (~12.3 s), so the modem
# came up at ~14.4 s and the card at ~18 s while the nano boot animation
# starts at ~6.7 s. Start the modem helpers at post-fs instead (right after the early mount_all
# that brings up the firmware and persist partitions; late-fs only ran at
# ~8.9 s here): pd-mapper and
# the peripheral manager need only /vendor and qrtr, rmt_storage the modem
# partitions, all of which are up by then. per_proxy (the modem vote) is
# started here as well: its stock per_mgr=running trigger was only serviced
# at ~13 s. irsc_util first: it installs the IPC router security rules; until
# it has run (stock: class core at boot, ~12.3 s) the QMI service registry
# traffic of pd-mapper (user system) is refused and the audio services stall.
on post-fs
    # Kernel firmware search path. /vendor/firmware holds the ADSP and CDSP
    # images this device actually runs (ueventd searches it first; the copy on
    # the firmware partition is an older build with different segment sizes,
    # so pointing the kernel there makes the ADSP fail with "truncated file").
    # With the path set, the ADSP segments and the smart-PA tuning load
    # directly instead of waiting for ueventd (the first segment waited ~1.7 s);
    # files not present there (the modem image) keep the ueventd fallback.
    write /sys/module/firmware_class/parameters/path /vendor/firmware
    # Pick the WL818S bridge firmware (default custom, or stock if the user chose
    # it) before the DP powers on and the kernel reads wl818s_fw.bin.
    exec_start vendor.wl818_select
    start irsc_util
    start vendor.tftp_server
    start vendor.pd_mapper
    start vendor.rmt_storage
    start vendor.per_mgr
    start vendor.per_proxy

# WL818S bridge firmware selector: redirects firmware_class.path to the stock
# backup when /mnt/vendor/persist/wl818/use_stock is 1, else the custom default.
# Run synchronously from post-fs (exec_start) so the choice is in place before
# the DP bring-up triggers fw_check.
service vendor.wl818_select /vendor/bin/wl818_select.sh
    class core
    user root
    group root system
    oneshot
    disabled

# Bridge firmware check brought forward to late-fs: opens the DRM node (the
# first open powers the DP, which runs the module's fw_check), watches the
# kernel log and, when this boot flashed the bridge, reboots once right away so
# the next boot brings the bottom panel up clean (the flashing boot leaves the
# DP erroring). It runs synchronously (exec_start) from hw/init.target.rc's
# late-fs block, right before mount_all --late mounts /data: a reboot during
# the first boot's data setup left the device in recovery ("Can't load Android
# system"), and there nothing of /data has been touched yet. The system's
# late-fs block has already started gammaos-nano, so the home is not delayed.
# It also does not wait for the long first boot after a factory reset or a
# fresh install.
service vendor.wl818_bootflash /vendor/bin/wl818_bootflash
    class core
    user root
    group root system graphics
    oneshot
    disabled

# Boot log keeper: the kernel log copied to /metadata/gammaos/boot_dmesg.txt every
# 2 s until boot completes, for boots that never reach adb or /data (see bootlog.sh).
service vendor.bootlog /vendor/bin/bootlog.sh
    class core
    user root
    group root system
    oneshot
    disabled

on post-fs
    start vendor.bootlog
